{
  "title": "Avascular Necrosis of the Shoulder",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3060/avascular-necrosis-of-the-shoulder",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 29 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Avascular necrosis of the shoulder is a condition characterized by interruption of blood supply to the humeral head which may lead to humeral head sclerosis and subchondral collapse.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made radiographically with orthogonal radiographs of the shoulder in moderate/late disease. MRI may be needed for detection of early or subclinical avascular necrosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be observation for very early and minimally symptomatic disease. Surgical management is indicated for progressive symptoms in the setting of moderate to advanced disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreased blood supply to humeral head leading to death of cells in bony matrix.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bone is resorbed and remodeled, causing **subchondral bone collapse** and may lead to joint incongruity and arthritic changes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "etiology similar to hip",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Remember **ASEPTIC** mneumonic",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**A**lcohol, **A**IDS",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Steroids (most common), Sickle**, **S**LE",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**E**rlenmeyer flask (Gaucher’s)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**P**ancreatitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**T**rauma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**I**diopathic/ Infection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**C**aisson’s (the bends)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**may be atraumatic**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**posttraumatic**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "four-part fracture-dislocations approach **100% AVN**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "displaced four-part fractures ~45% AVN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "valgus impacted four-part ~11% AVN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "three-part ~14% AVN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Blood supply",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Humeral head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**ascending branch** of **anterior humeral circumflex artery** and **arcuate artery**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "provides blood supply to humeral head",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "vessel runs parallel to lateral aspect of tendon of long head of biceps in the bicipital groove",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "beware not to injure when plating proximal humerus fractures",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "arcuate artery is the interosseous continuation of ascending branch of anterior humeral circumflex artery and penetrates the bone of the humeral head",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "provides 35% of blood supply to humeral head",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**posterior humeral circumflex artery**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**most current literature** supports this as providing the **main blood supply to humeral head**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "provides 65% of blood supply",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
